// An exit code must fit a signed 32-bit integer, and an Int is a code as a
// Number is (spec/05-stdlib.md, exit). An Int above the range is a runtime
// error that halts the program, so the exit code is not 1 or 0: the halt
// status is non-zero and no CHECK line binds it.
// STATUS: error
// CHECK: before
print "before";
exit(2147483648i);
print "unreachable";
